{"objects":[{"id":"flow","instance":"instance--b96dad5f-c519-5a1f-a718-912ca4a86c02","objects":["attack-action--1","attack-action--2","attack-action--3","attack-action--4","attack-action--5","attack-action--6","attack-action--7","attack-action--8","attack-action--9","attack-action--10","attack-action--11","attack-condition--1","attack-operator--1","software--1","software--2","software--3","software--4","software--5","software--6","instance--c28a235a-e55f-5315-957a-585a68fea246","instance--a3be7850-59e6-5377-b9f4-8238ce03a1d2","instance--ad1f125b-7701-5e9d-b869-79f40471648d","instance--384798bd-a84b-5feb-8d38-7f9d0a087f11","instance--ed6039fe-678b-5ae9-9576-73e6ea35b0c8","instance--d10376f5-8e18-5fa1-93e0-8fa9e55f61b1","instance--b4f8976f-808a-599a-879a-cb9df667a777","instance--3622ace1-abf1-5f6e-a5de-a6f584dc1f66","instance--56b40d44-cc57-5e8b-b320-779a685089fd","instance--895aab9a-87c3-51d8-91f8-cc3f6dd1a5a5","instance--3bb881aa-a5ab-51ba-b53d-89d26964ce7d","instance--be99ba49-e121-58a8-ba7b-dd3de316cfcf","instance--56da8838-1109-5fce-9d89-7b3ec32d7010","instance--d110b130-8c28-5cb4-98a0-76aaa8233093","instance--e28c61d0-be08-595d-b694-80935ffe4433","instance--e48436f9-eef5-5df1-ae6b-a83c9fb04c9f","instance--471cd0ba-bcd7-5a60-bf2e-a2594276cafe","instance--758b8a34-ff0e-5daa-b9c0-f4f91307f4fb","instance--9f2f8919-9f0c-50a2-aa32-bbf6bb95407b","instance--d44bbc06-16eb-59e7-ad26-f4789470a21b","instance--e97a2eed-2ebb-5149-872b-ebf61e991ccf","instance--fece5f21-45a1-51e3-84d5-d2729deb9aa6","instance--a7e0986d-5cda-57b6-95f1-53d649a1938b"],"properties":[["name","A Death Match of Domain Generation Algorithms"],["description","The article describes attacker use of domain generation algorithms to hide command-and-control infrastructure and evade detection."],["scope","campaign"],["author",[["name","Yuriy Yuzifovich"]]],["external_references",[["item-1",[["source_name","medium.com"],["url","https://medium.com/@yvyuz/a-death-match-of-domain-generation-algorithms-a5b5dbdc1c6e"]]]]]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--ad592d05-6969-5b51-98a8-1ad9b6aab896","120":"instance--5850a8f4-8241-5e73-9bf0-dcd376cd5025","150":"instance--0da1498f-3beb-5916-a249-e0410a4a81e4","180":"instance--d3632784-7391-5a29-83e2-edab51db56c6","210":"instance--8bc47ca5-ca73-5a04-a9ea-918608f10871","240":"instance--6546eef6-c5ad-516e-a417-89916e651648","270":"instance--244e5a69-f465-564e-9d2c-93d4da44fc57","30":"instance--6a1fca3c-fdb6-536a-bbea-61ac2349a700","300":"instance--043a5b44-2864-5565-abce-1909204e5485","330":"instance--e10eb918-2b0b-56f4-9c82-f345ce21276c","60":"instance--33a99d1b-dad8-51f6-be74-e1614db9151b","90":"instance--380c79e9-b1eb-547c-bf01-a011db1201c1"},"id":"action","instance":"attack-action--1","properties":[["name","Generate DGA candidate domains"],["description","The general methodology of any DGA is using a deterministic pseudo-random generator (PRNG) to generate a list of candidate domain names. The seed of a PRNG can be the current date, some magic numbers, an exchange rate, etc. This random generator can be a single uniform distribution generator, e.g. use a combination of bitshift, xor, divide, multiply, and modulo operations to generate a string sequence as the domain name (such as in Conficker, Ramnit, and others); it can also be a rule generator, which selects from some knowledge base (such as in Suppobox)."],["confidence",0.0],["ttp",{"tactic":"TA0011","technique":"T1568.002"}]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--4f4d03a8-4502-5010-997b-9943e254395b","120":"instance--cefe62ac-5b6e-5ead-84fc-b4c632913a73","150":"instance--4d07a740-2467-5b95-ac8d-4a2ee8edd11e","180":"instance--1205f03c-a457-5a0b-87ef-3bbb7aac110f","210":"instance--96e7dc6a-9f86-5f69-8d45-a566303cd4c0","240":"instance--66237af6-bb19-5a51-9fa2-cbc4a96186f5","270":"instance--836dfd42-b475-50ca-9acf-4f11bd32b89f","30":"instance--efe92997-cc5c-538a-90bc-c09ffb1379f4","300":"instance--9c4a24ae-1426-5cb5-9d7c-792e6dd325b7","330":"instance--06c6a74a-ca7d-5703-88ea-a06a0933d21a","60":"instance--5e4f84e5-56b7-5b8f-9bc3-b4d59d371123","90":"instance--019deb6a-bab3-57db-9a53-11e3564bf7a4"},"id":"action","instance":"attack-action--2","properties":[["name","Select DGA domains for C2 service"],["description","The key to the PRNG-based DGA methodology is a deterministic random generator, where the DGA sequence is predictable from both the malware and the attacker, so the attacker can generate and select some of these domains for C&C service, and the malware just needs to loop over and reach the chosen C&C."],["confidence",0.0],["ttp",{"tactic":"TA0011","technique":"T1568.002"}]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--0ce35aea-35a2-52ae-a67b-985306bdefe7","120":"instance--312639d5-e6d9-57b1-850d-28f0a1eac2f6","150":"instance--9551a25e-2558-512e-9894-dd64a8d662bf","180":"instance--403becce-e0ad-5dcd-bc14-7c00453907da","210":"instance--2305f501-2712-5ec6-9d4e-1371b011e937","240":"instance--cf1b8cf6-1cbd-5afb-b653-aa693889dab5","270":"instance--1d3dc59a-40a0-5670-aa3e-1304ff762003","30":"instance--77063d4f-503a-5e9b-b622-15aa2cc6a8e7","300":"instance--beaab67f-8a54-5982-8c5d-9d2ed2d42c9f","330":"instance--4d3274ff-ef14-5a53-99be-01575194a98e","60":"instance--4154a6bf-290b-5fce-a557-5dc0f3e700fb","90":"instance--2992bc0b-df57-54e5-a17b-03a964338c09"},"id":"action","instance":"attack-action--3","properties":[["name","Loop over generated names to reach C2"],["description","The key to the PRNG-based DGA methodology is a deterministic random generator, where the DGA sequence is predictable from both the malware and the attacker, so the attacker can generate and select some of these domains for C&C service, and the malware just needs to loop over and reach the chosen C&C."],["confidence",0.0],["ttp",{"tactic":"TA0011","technique":"T1071.004"}]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--0f6e4da7-a5f4-54d7-866f-3bc6e8bcb019","120":"instance--015254b5-0906-577e-b3e3-3899f837d118","150":"instance--f7af5b8c-330a-58d5-b0da-a3d5f0bc6ad0","180":"instance--9f27ab21-2382-567d-b022-74ad5a29bd08","210":"instance--d799eb0a-7600-5b1a-a298-c47a78ceae4b","240":"instance--911c2c52-5974-5e08-b0b6-a9084d57c6ee","270":"instance--286444b4-97a1-58cd-9ca3-cffa04a15351","30":"instance--92192c38-5143-50e0-8c39-a96ea86e32e2","300":"instance--82bb3de0-bea5-5651-a1de-583283258c6d","330":"instance--4f0945c8-f644-50ce-8796-fea52a29dda1","60":"instance--16c43a2d-7356-521d-a507-5922e2c3337b","90":"instance--abce5c62-339a-5ed5-a0b8-dd66136cfe2f"},"id":"action","instance":"attack-action--4","properties":[["name","Use date and magic numbers as dynamic seeds"],["description","Since the attacker\u2019s goal is to avoid detection, it becomes practical to use magic numbers as dynamic seeds. The magic number technique is very common today, and Necurs (the backdoor), Locky (the ransomware) ( https://test-nominum.pantheonsite.io/unlocking-locky/) are good examples of the combined usage of date/time and magic numbers. Magic numbers are usually combined with the date in bit-shifting and provide additional variance. Popular malware like Locky can deploy many variants with different magic numbers each to evade detection"],["confidence",0.0],["ttp",{"tactic":"TA0011","technique":"T1568.002"}]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--a469636c-0cb2-50b9-92f9-644c8aa98197","120":"instance--d57b3a21-e910-5879-8148-40165cea451a","150":"instance--58250ef4-5bb4-5bf3-b33e-89493bbb395d","180":"instance--3e769cf2-c1e5-5d2e-81d4-892f48ce4d86","210":"instance--f6499e41-749c-5d7f-9346-96c08d0d5dfd","240":"instance--d9dcdfc8-5f42-546a-803a-0efcd5d4cf91","270":"instance--c9afd0f6-97ce-57b2-9d60-3557b6214809","30":"instance--75f82155-f5ff-5619-8bf8-aae22937cab0","300":"instance--25e2d26e-1b35-56bd-b9aa-096c2d3b0e3c","330":"instance--e0483688-da10-5376-8cf2-050bcc3b70f0","60":"instance--1293d9cc-16b2-5c67-a453-bd144aab133a","90":"instance--2b43cd52-10db-5b15-8ad5-c4b59496528b"},"id":"action","instance":"attack-action--5","properties":[["name","Use currency exchange rate as seed"],["description","The exchange rate of currency can be used as random seeds. Bedep the Ad/Click fraud botnet, for example, use foreign currency exchange rate as their seed"],["confidence",0.0],["ttp",{"tactic":"TA0011","technique":"T1568.002"}]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--54fc1f38-f4e3-523e-b07c-73889b0d8df7","120":"instance--9cf45948-7040-5d7a-a1d5-3cb4db0c1af6","150":"instance--13bb13cc-e02b-51d2-8d7d-40e5613b6e5a","180":"instance--e33bc6ee-771e-54fe-a772-74dfdaad420d","210":"instance--286f51a3-8fc6-55ec-978e-8b05ebda3655","240":"instance--14659696-be77-5460-beb1-4b5eac126e43","270":"instance--f48ed1a6-2895-5cd2-9b1c-e30ac2bc8921","30":"instance--7b803e61-16ac-5720-92cd-8f2a456a52b7","300":"instance--76c24361-5143-5c43-8e4d-707c619e6038","330":"instance--f395cfc7-395a-5001-9552-a4fec6dbc53a","60":"instance--760885bb-9294-5a5b-93a2-a410e1ea4112","90":"instance--8e0d1a12-8611-598d-9a7d-40f2525e4781"},"id":"action","instance":"attack-action--6","properties":[["name","Use Twitter hashtag as seed"],["description","Some botnets use the most popular hashtag on twitter as the DGA seed, as reported by Cybereason"],["confidence",0.0],["ttp",{"tactic":"TA0011","technique":"T1568.002"}]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--7cccbcd0-a724-54fb-be4f-ac523d26f7d0","120":"instance--738e44b2-1357-5eb3-82bd-8a0ce8942b72","150":"instance--d31f4735-6339-5929-8d7c-d30863cf166f","180":"instance--2252393d-d801-5931-ad38-4b53374a9880","210":"instance--065b5ad5-023a-5336-b458-e9c9dcda2976","240":"instance--5ea0dd2b-5eac-51f8-855a-4cbcb801bc2d","270":"instance--bba66874-a069-56c6-bb95-967cb3cefc9e","30":"instance--6377c09d-ecb4-5567-a2f4-4dde56ff4f98","300":"instance--ede3430f-b16b-58ae-be71-1d1f1a194336","330":"instance--7772f482-8ee2-569a-b600-7528c065d4e0","60":"instance--98139a98-16b0-54fe-8c77-3473c1b520cd","90":"instance--5cb9cc95-e190-5a68-985d-0a94d39299e6"},"id":"action","instance":"attack-action--7","properties":[["name","Use dictionary words in generated domains"],["description","Some cleverly designed DGAs such as Suppobox try to evade this randomness by using dictionary words:"],["confidence",0.0],["ttp",{"tactic":"TA0011","technique":"T1568.002"}]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--5150f7cc-6f25-5eb3-a6fc-5099ced4caf4","120":"instance--64a408ce-c543-55d6-a9dd-206ce7cadbb2","150":"instance--1b71e413-cfd2-528c-8792-dc7dd1bb9938","180":"instance--aa12ce11-0165-52b6-b72d-e4d9070e9fbb","210":"instance--5d8b0f08-14bc-58f4-9316-b25a92dd09a6","240":"instance--34f96b84-9453-53f2-ae07-d28c04665e6c","270":"instance--415f1d54-1cd4-5ba7-8071-4aa99bc946ac","30":"instance--18834cac-b4c4-57b0-88ea-5a62fdb27cf9","300":"instance--de4f9957-1ac6-5782-86ea-f1a3b6a9ad13","330":"instance--8eff940b-86bb-556f-8c85-c7c47577b3ed","60":"instance--14a123fd-5626-5e69-8257-6dcd64c28ec0","90":"instance--02294ff1-7261-5db8-8e0d-b9e818922053"},"id":"action","instance":"attack-action--8","properties":[["name","Flood recursive DNS traffic with generated domains"],["description","Pykspa is a worm whose DGA is reverse-engineered at . This DGA generates thousands of possible DGA domains using common TLDs like com, biz, net, org, info and cc, and its core domain has 6\u201315 chars. These thousands of domains flood the recursive DNS traffic."],["confidence",0.0],["ttp",{"tactic":"TA0011","technique":"T1568.002"}]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--180f2983-9c1a-56f4-99d6-c990125f7baa","120":"instance--c7f65318-7600-57f4-a8ac-992357e695ff","150":"instance--95523e1a-0a1d-52ef-944c-23f9cbc50233","180":"instance--bc8eb48d-411d-5877-aa9b-966476b71207","210":"instance--4cc5026e-07f9-5327-9912-5d278a0a3321","240":"instance--d6a7d51d-39a4-5eb3-8831-f23437781b95","270":"instance--cac30e05-5f01-5b4f-b5c0-6b975297df2d","30":"instance--cb0751b0-c027-5895-a460-a72e48920c71","300":"instance--f41cdc1f-abb7-5ff7-81c2-bf2235a7faab","330":"instance--b114cbda-9ec8-5612-b2f8-93c36811cafb","60":"instance--f28e5296-2041-5fe9-992d-4c70d549191e","90":"instance--3ea39244-da0f-5435-8745-f2afa8b13872"},"id":"action","instance":"attack-action--9","properties":[["name","Generate short six-character domains"],["description","Virut is another type of DGA where the domain name only has 6 a-z chars with TLD, and the algorithm itself has a simplistic design, so the chance of a generated domain colliding with a legitimate service is very high."],["confidence",0.0],["ttp",{"tactic":"TA0011","technique":"T1568.002"}]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--db5fab04-54d4-5eec-a429-185861eb2719","120":"instance--985391bd-d017-5935-ab31-3b4b56331b02","150":"instance--092bb98d-fc30-5f69-b6b7-e3024f3ec65a","180":"instance--755129e6-612e-5b63-a780-1c886d98909b","210":"instance--431723d9-dd8c-5190-9dab-6f346173c044","240":"instance--5b9fb821-54fe-5f22-bba3-038263245910","270":"instance--3c6777cb-6430-544b-b31a-01b198524553","30":"instance--c070071b-a9a3-52fe-8956-a51744db200b","300":"instance--a9a4289c-d995-5783-9544-a8b45052eb56","330":"instance--344009cc-e024-5c68-9246-51e85e00d45c","60":"instance--86c77621-2c1d-59c3-b398-e62f4b48a3dd","90":"instance--67627b08-1913-5f3d-8318-52d3bda9c1c3"},"id":"action","instance":"attack-action--10","properties":[["name","Hardcode domain lists in binary"],["description","instead of a DGA, the author has hardcoded them in the binary and deployed different lists in different binaries. These names are used in Ruskill/Dorkbot as reported at and ."],["confidence",0.0],["ttp",{"tactic":"TA0005","technique":"T1027.011"}]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--6b7baffd-afaf-5472-9af2-a263119a77ef","120":"instance--83f38e63-e29a-53f4-99d9-927a195c453f","150":"instance--3e720145-b7a1-5bd6-8a7d-bb13519675d1","180":"instance--bdce060f-d96c-5b06-b8f4-1ab1527fd01d","210":"instance--a4feb251-e6e3-5680-a712-d59c92f73ccf","240":"instance--9a564ca6-b753-5b06-880c-b3aac25c1e73","270":"instance--76861a89-f006-5e0d-8c5b-ebdcb5e926dc","30":"instance--cf41e64d-4a4b-58d9-9962-72d278b2c489","300":"instance--ac1d6edd-482f-5f13-9348-b605afcc260c","330":"instance--ed78dfa1-f300-564f-b2cd-6c99552b9a68","60":"instance--979accb3-1b3e-5af4-9182-78392cbaf904","90":"instance--ae721c42-320e-5ea4-9c77-339a05b6e12f"},"id":"action","instance":"attack-action--11","properties":[["name","Generate decoy names every 10 seconds"],["description","there is an ongoing discussion here about the DGA behind Dorkbot, where Johannes Bader has commented that Dorkbot generates these names every 10 seconds and uses as decoys."],["confidence",0.0],["ttp",{"tactic":"TA0011","technique":"T1568.002"}]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--35652c79-2c41-5d60-81ba-b5e47aa554bf","120":"instance--53906203-fffb-5af3-b112-44a9b4b49b8f","150":"instance--465fbc8a-7b4c-569f-be00-c0fbc137fcfc","180":"instance--a653c96b-3673-5dfa-968e-188fffe4cc04","210":"instance--6a344cf5-bd5c-52db-84f5-23c7701c7a5e","30":"instance--913561d1-b5f3-54d2-8272-159233dfde54","330":"instance--d59fe52d-c897-5f3a-919a-c2273cb8a8b3","60":"instance--f1fd6a3d-bb83-543d-a379-39d4632978f7","90":"instance--4cd6fce2-0d24-57f0-b161-12a867cd1100","branch:False":"instance--f7e897b3-3607-5ea5-8d15-5f83ba8a60da","branch:True":"instance--39b5ac19-b0dd-5674-a7d9-d75e659fe9ea"},"id":"condition","instance":"attack-condition--1","properties":[["description","This part requires some agreement: both the DGA and the seed must be known by both sides before generating DGA domains."]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--36aad375-d405-5e3b-9a7d-4346c75c9f45","120":"instance--acc72955-e581-59b3-80b5-35fb047df4b8","150":"instance--d5d0ec7c-da1b-5d39-86e4-8de8792ab05d","180":"instance--047e7862-d9c4-5716-b778-899a86595b48","210":"instance--650a6d3c-5cb0-5f82-83ec-c5d828e2502b","240":"instance--3f08654d-fd5e-59cb-af47-8bbcee29de39","270":"instance--e175549d-38ff-5527-bdb8-de5e1a12f356","30":"instance--c6e60459-b005-50cd-9e68-66ef210b5456","300":"instance--f90b34f0-8620-5a56-9e11-4db2b889aac4","330":"instance--93872aee-cf81-52fa-aa93-f7a84a833dbd","60":"instance--5a877a06-3649-5bba-9461-5faee75ea842","90":"instance--68af6616-0e27-5395-b4ff-5d95b55a2405"},"id":"OR_operator","instance":"attack-operator--1","properties":[["operator","OR"]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--905f37ff-524a-522a-8685-08b6df9b34bd","120":"instance--a0b8bf42-8310-53d9-87f0-390378638ae9","150":"instance--ffafa2fa-6430-5714-9c5e-bbf977c9819b","180":"instance--10bf0e4d-ac4d-5742-b82b-398ef2467e2a","210":"instance--f2066b53-6fa4-5efa-8f61-dc81d3df5b0e","240":"instance--fbb6b151-c9f4-5cb6-b467-c563cc0c60d3","270":"instance--451ff5e8-5cc8-5d6c-b701-da17c04936f7","30":"instance--059bc992-da53-5d4b-ac82-60cfacc08e81","300":"instance--1d241382-a8ee-554a-aa3a-04366535b315","330":"instance--8a7078e9-787d-56b2-a734-f93cd76b3dc8","60":"instance--8aab1831-f6e3-582d-8f9b-3ad920a40e35","90":"instance--192458e5-76c8-5d8c-ab54-9ed8b36ef2bd"},"id":"software","instance":"software--1","properties":[["evidence",[["item-1",{"excerpt":"Necurs (the backdoor), Locky (the ransomware)","source":"https://medium.com/@yvyuz/a-death-match-of-domain-generation-algorithms-a5b5dbdc1c6e","source_field":"normalized_text"}]]],["display_name","Necurs"],["name","Necurs"]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--7bca99b4-fc37-5b67-9da4-7aaaaca1937e","120":"instance--a653e288-958c-5a34-826a-c7ae2da3173f","150":"instance--9fb91ed2-00e9-50c3-8ceb-3f10b07b73bc","180":"instance--bf4d856a-43b2-58e9-a272-467b1a321907","210":"instance--10ca6953-dd7d-54b7-9406-bb40125e27e2","240":"instance--db0c8479-7e26-5d86-b4d9-d52f19ad3f45","270":"instance--3f9b75b2-1c8a-564a-8a7b-b898a27995dd","30":"instance--3663489e-5635-5e70-b0e5-70a502523b87","300":"instance--bdba1e6c-e0e6-5e31-a7d0-c53e76e3cb8b","330":"instance--163f5749-44cf-50b1-ba73-97edab024b3b","60":"instance--7d417c1a-591b-5278-821e-7d21ac26d33f","90":"instance--4d5c0684-fd37-55f3-860f-2e9735603afe"},"id":"software","instance":"software--2","properties":[["evidence",[["item-1",{"excerpt":"Necurs (the backdoor), Locky (the ransomware)","source":"https://medium.com/@yvyuz/a-death-match-of-domain-generation-algorithms-a5b5dbdc1c6e","source_field":"normalized_text"}]]],["display_name","Locky"],["name","Locky"]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance